WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:04.620
The Mother of Dragons hasn't been the same
since she conquered Westeros . Ever since

00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:09.160
Emilia Clarke wrapped up her role as Daenerys
Targaryen on HBO's hit series Game of Thrones,

00:00:09.460 --> 00:00:13.480
she has spoken out about some of the tougher
moments she faced both on and off screen.

00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:18.039
Throughout aher incredibly challenging, decade-long
role, the actress survived plenty of harrowing

00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:20.780
times, no matter how much fame and acclaim
she racked up.

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:24.960
In the time since Game of Thrones came to
a fiery conclusion, Emilia Clarke has been

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:28.420
extraordinarily forthcoming about some of
the biggest struggles she dealt with during

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:28.920
filming.

00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:33.640
In short, it's not hard to understand why
she hasn't fully recovered from Game of Thrones.

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:38.690
As a fresh-faced star on a huge HBO show,
Emilia Clarke seemed destined for stardom

00:00:38.690 --> 00:00:40.660
thanks to her performance as Daenerys.

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:45.480
However, it wasn't until the spring of 2019
that fans realized just how much personal

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:47.580
comfort she truly sacrificed for the role.

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:51.800
In a New Yorker piece that ran in March of
that year, Clarke admitted that she suffered

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:55.999
two debilitating brain injuries while filming
the first two seasons of Game of Thrones,

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:58.640
both of which could have ended her career
and life.

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:03.100
After experiencing a serious brain aneurysm
right after she wrapped filming on the show's

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:07.500
freshman season, Clarke thankfully recovered,
but was left frightened, depressed, and anxious

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:09.940
about whether or not she would be able to
continue working.

00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:14.880
The actress suffered from aphasia, a condition
that renders one unable to speak correctly,

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:16.440
in the aftermath of the first aneurysm.

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:21.280
During the show's second season, she suffered
from serious anxiety and collapsed once, then

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:24.940
endured yet another aneurysm after the third
season of Thrones wrapped.

00:01:25.180 --> 00:01:29.700
At that time, Clarke was also preparing for
her Broadway debut in Breakfast at Tiffany's.

00:01:29.880 --> 00:01:34.579
Clarke's co-stars, including Khal Drogo actor
Jason Momoa, were incredibly supportive of

00:01:34.579 --> 00:01:38.369
her speaking out about what she had been through,
but the experience was terrifying for the

00:01:38.369 --> 00:01:39.160
young actress.

00:01:39.640 --> 00:01:43.180
In the same article, Clarke revealed that
she sank to a dark place after her second

00:01:43.180 --> 00:01:43.900
aneurysm:

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:45.520
"All hope receded.

00:01:45.620 --> 00:01:47.360
I felt like a shell of myself.

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:51.340
So much so that I now have a hard time remembering
those dark days in much detail.

00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:52.740
My mind has blocked them out.

00:01:53.260 --> 00:01:55.940
But I do remember being convinced that I wasn't
going to live."

00:01:56.460 --> 00:02:01.159
Beyond her frightening offscreen medical struggles,
Emilia Clarke also endured plenty of hardships

00:02:01.160 --> 00:02:02.500
on the set of Game of Thrones.

00:02:03.020 --> 00:02:07.900
As a star of a show that was routinely called
out for unnecessary nudity, Clarke was unsurprisingly

00:02:07.900 --> 00:02:09.840
asked to perform a number of nude scenes.

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:14.940
She was often uncomfortable on set and unsure
if she could say no until later seasons, once

00:02:14.940 --> 00:02:16.860
she gained more clout and recognition.

00:02:17.260 --> 00:02:21.600
In November 2019, she admitted that some of
her nude scenes were difficult to handle,

00:02:21.610 --> 00:02:25.390
particularly because she felt both powerless
and pressured as a young performer on the

00:02:25.390 --> 00:02:27.080
cusp of international stardom.

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:31.740
However, with or without the nude scenes,
Clarke also suffered from serious imposter

00:02:31.740 --> 00:02:34.780
syndrome on the set of Thrones during the
show's early seasons.

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:37.780
As she told Dax Shepard on his podcast Armchair
Expert:

00:02:38.360 --> 00:02:42.220
"Regardless of if there were nudity or not,
I would have spent that first season thinking,

00:02:42.220 --> 00:02:47.000
'I'm not worthy of requiring anything, I'm
not worthy of needing anything at all."

00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:51.680
Beyond that, Daenerys Targaryen's journey
left Emilia Clarke understandably shaken as

00:02:51.680 --> 00:02:52.180
well.

00:02:52.460 --> 00:02:56.640
The actress spent years playing her character
as a virtuous, justice-driven young queen

00:02:56.640 --> 00:02:59.480
hell-bent on reclaiming her family's ancestral
throne.

00:02:59.600 --> 00:03:03.540
That's why it shocked Clarke just as much
as anyone else when Daenerys torched King's

00:03:03.540 --> 00:03:06.480
Landing from atop her largest dragon in the
final season.

00:03:07.280 --> 00:03:11.000
The decision led to her murdering countless
innocent civilians in her quest to take the

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:11.800
Iron Throne.

00:03:12.380 --> 00:03:15.640
Clarke admitted that upon reading the script
and learning of the big Daenerys twist, she

00:03:15.640 --> 00:03:19.860
had to walk around the streets of London just
to process the character's personal arc.

00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:24.850
That shock was undoubtedly made even worse,
considering that after sacking King's Landing,

00:03:24.850 --> 00:03:26.880
Dany doesn't make it to the Iron Throne.

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:30.260
Instead, she's assassinated by her nephew-lover
Jon Snow.

00:03:30.880 --> 00:03:35.320
Clarke will likely always be associated with
Daenerys Targaryen, but even Game of Thrones'

00:03:35.320 --> 00:03:39.650
biggest fans should recognize the sacrifices
the actor made for this enormous, unforgettable

00:03:39.660 --> 00:03:40.160
role.

